      en: "Nagarjun is a municipality in the western part of the Kathmandu Valley, known for its lush forests and spiritual significance. A large portion of the municipality is covered by the Nagarjun Forest, which is part of the Shivapuri-Nagarjun National Park and serves as a crucial habitat for urban wildlife and a vital green lung for the valley. The forest is named after the Buddhist philosopher Nagarjuna, who is believed to have meditated here. The summit of Nagarjun Hill features a Buddhist gompa and a view tower offering panoramic vistas of Kathmandu and the surrounding mountains. The municipality combines quiet residential areas with the pristine nature of the national park, making it a popular spot for hikers, birdwatchers, and pilgrims."
